# ============================================================================
#  VoIPAppz portal — environment
#  Copy to `.env` and fill in:   cp .env.example .env   (or: make env)
#  A tenant fork changes ENV, not code.
#
#  Pure BEAM: connectix/ is the whole app, and every variable below is read by
#  it (connectix/config/runtime.exs, via Connectix.Config). There is no
#  frontend build to configure separately — no VITE_* namespace exists.
# ============================================================================

# ── Production fallback: which mothership this tenant talks to ──────────────
# Used by the local production Compose profile when ENGINE_URL is unset.
MOTHERSHIP_URL=https://cloud.voipappz.io

# Everything below is OPTIONAL — the app runs with just the line above.

# ── Local portal → API resolution (dev only) ─────────────────────────────────
# PORTAL_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000      # local portal → local API
# CABLE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000          # local cable → the same API
# ENGINE_URL — production portal override when MOTHERSHIP_URL is not the engine.

# ── The portal (connectix, :4001) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole app: it serves the LiveView UI and /ws/events, PERFORMS the login,
# verifies its own tokens, consumes events straight off NATS through Broadway,
# and forwards the rest of /auth, /api/ and /tasks/ upstream.
#
# THE CABLE IS GONE. There is no ActionCable hop, no CABLE_* variable and no
# token round trip to anyone: Elixir holds the NATS connection itself.
# NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222
#
# What to consume, when the rule file names no subjects. `*` matches any ONE
# token, which is every colon-form stream at once; `state.>` is every state
# stream. NATS splits on dots alone, so a colon-form name is a single token.
# NATS_SUBJECTS=*,state.>
#
# THE CUSTOMER'S RULE IS NOT A VARIABLE. docker-compose.yml mounts
# connectix/priv/pocketflow/customers/<site>.yaml at /rules/screen_pop.yaml,
# and production mounts /etc/connectix/screen_pop.yaml at the same path. The
# file that is mounted IS the customer — its subjects, its agents, its CRM URL.
#
# What the agents in that file sign in with. The file names the variable and
# never holds the value: a password committed once stays in the history after
# the file stops carrying it.
# AGENT_PASSWORD=
#
# Local DuckDB audit history for received Cable frames. EVENTS_DB overrides the
# directory and should point at a mounted volume when history must survive a
# container replacement. This store is observational; failure never stops events.
# EVENTS_DIR=                                 # default: <CONNECTIX_DATA_DIR>/events
# EVENTS_DB=                                  # default: <EVENTS_DIR>/events.duckdb
# Extra `state.<scope>.<id>` streams the ONE application cable connection
# subscribes to, purely so their frames are stored. `scope:id`, comma-separated.
# Cable has no firehose: CallEvents is node-wide, but everything else lives on
# `state.<scope>.<id>` and StateChannel requires BOTH halves — so an unnamed
# stream is an unwatched one, and an empty store cannot distinguish "the node
# sent nothing" from "we were not listening".
# Scopes: user, queue, call, environment, campaign, conference, extension.
# EVENT_STREAMS=environment:<uuid>,user:<uuid>
#
# Log shipping: the portal's log lines go to InfluxDB 3 as well as stdout —
# stdout stays exactly as it is (Kamal reads it), Influx is for querying.
# The SAME names va-crystal's node reads, so one .env configures both. The
# token is the switch: unset, no handler is installed and nothing is posted.
# Best effort — an unreachable InfluxDB is one warning at boot, never a crash.
# VA_MONITOR_TOKEN=                           # bearer; unset = log shipping off
# VA_INFLUXDB_HOST=influxdb                   # 127.0.0.1 from a host-network container
# VA_INFLUXDB_PORT=8181
# VA_INFLUXDB_DATABASE=telegraf
#
# NO DATABASE. The portal dropped Ecto in 39c92198: durable state is Mnesia
# (MNESIA_DIR) and the DuckDB event store (EVENTS_DIR), both under
# CONNECTIX_DATA_DIR. PGHOST/DATABASE_URL are read by nothing.
#
# MNESIA_DIR IS WHAT MAKES IT DURABLE. Unset, Mnesia runs ram_copies and every
# restart is a fresh, empty, perfectly healthy-looking database.
# CONNECTIX_DATA_DIR=/data
# SECRET_KEY_BASE=                            # production; `mix phx.gen.secret`

# ── Agent chat LiveView UI (Elixir, optional) ────────────────────────────────
# `/` and `/chat` are always compiled in (no build-time flag); this is the
# only real gate. Unset, the UI is reachable with no credential — fine for
# local dev, never for a shared box. There is one operator identity: the
# username IS the account.
# PORTAL_UI_USER=
# PORTAL_UI_PASS=

# ── Deploy / ops ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROD_URL=https://your-host                  # `make status` health probe target
